   "explain": "The heat removed from inside plus the electrical work are both released into the room."
  }
 ],
 "takeaways": [
  "A **refrigerator** is a heat engine **run in reverse**: work in, heat pumped from cold to hot.",
  "\\( Q_h = Q_c + W \\) and \\( CP = Q_c/W \\).",
  "The **second law** says it cannot work without a supply of work."
 ],
 "notes": [
  {
   "title": "Connects to",
   "text": "Run the **Carnot cycle** backwards (anticlockwise on the P–V graph) and you get the **ideal refrigerator**. It is the second-law (Clausius) statement in action."
  }
 ]
